<%# The trail, as markup a reader can use and a crawler can read.

  The JSON-LD BreadcrumbList that mirrors it is built from the SAME array, beside this render
  (marketing/shared/_page.html.erb), so the structured data cannot describe a trail the page does not show.
  This is the visible half, and it is the reason a detail page is not a dead end on a phone, where the
  header navigation is one row of five links.

  The last item carries aria-current and no href: a link to the page you are already on is noise for a screen
  reader and a self-referential internal link for a crawler.

  THREE THINGS, AND THEY LOOK LIKE THREE THINGS. The trail used to be one undifferentiated grey run: the links
  carried the same colour as the current page, and the separator was set in `text-lyn-line` -- the hairline
  token, 1.24:1 on paper, which is a surface colour and not readable type. The link now takes the paper link
  accent, the separator sits between the two, and where you are is the darkest and the only weighted crumb.

  AND THE LINKS ARE REAL TAP TARGETS. They were ~16px tall on the one component whose entire job is getting
  out of a detail page on a phone. The anchors take the 44px control floor through vertical padding, and the
  row pulls that padding back off with a negative margin, so a reader gets the target without the trail
  growing into a band.
%>
<nav aria-label="<%= t('marketing.breadcrumb') %>" class="mb-6 text-xs text-lyn-ink-soft">
  <ol class="-my-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5">
    <% trail.each_with_index do |crumb, index| %>
      <li class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <% if index.positive? %>
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-lyn-ink-soft/50">/</span>
        <% end %>
        <% if crumb[:path] %>
          <a class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center py-3 text-lyn-royal transition-colors hover:text-lyn-ink focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-lyn-blue"
             href="<%= crumb[:path] %>"><%= crumb[:label] %></a>
        <% else %>
          <span aria-current="page" class="font-medium text-lyn-ink"><%= crumb[:label] %></span>
        <% end %>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ol>
</nav>
